sub_0200C628 / sub_0200C630 (the sprite wrappers' "get animation frame")
are void here but return sub_0202022C's frame on the ROM: mwcc compiles the
void body to the same `bl sub_0202022C; pop {pc}` that leaves the frame in
r0, and every assembly caller reads it (ov11_02250338, the trainer's ball
throw, waits for frame 3 to release the Poke Ball; ov08_02226B2C,
ov08_02228B08, ov75_021EC3B8). The wasm bridge returns 0 from a void C
function, so the throw never let go of the ball and the first battle stalled
on "Go! TURTWIG!" (pc/tools/dp_voidret_lint.py finds this class). Both now
return the frame; render_window.c already declares sub_0202022C u32.

